{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Skyscraper is an upcoming roller coaster that will be located at the planned Skyplex complex in Orlando, Florida.","title":"Skyscraper (roller coaster)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Under development by American and Swiss manufacturers US Thrill Rides and Intamin, the attraction will be a Polercoaster model which utilizes an observation tower as its main support structure.","title":"Skyscraper (roller coaster)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" After several delays, Skyscraper is expected to open in 2020 with construction on the Skyplex complex beginning in 2017.","title":"Skyscraper (roller coaster)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Upon completion, it will become the tallest roller coaster in the world at over 500 ft and will feature both the steepest drop and highest inversion.","title":"Skyscraper (roller coaster)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Millennium Force is a steel roller coaster built by Intamin at Cedar Point amusement park in Sandusky, Ohio, United States.","title":"Millennium Force"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was the fourteenth roller coaster to be built at the park since Blue Streak opened in 1964.","title":"Millennium Force"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Upon completion in 2000, Millennium Force broke six world records and was the world's first Giga Coaster, a roller coaster that exceeds 300 ft in height and completes a full circuit.","title":"Millennium Force"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It was briefly the tallest and fastest in the world until Steel Dragon 2000 opened later the same year.","title":"Millennium Force"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The ride is also the third-longest roller coaster in North America after The Beast at Kings Island and Fury 325 at Carowinds.","title":"Millennium Force"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" It was the first roller coaster to use a cable lift system rather than a traditional chain lift.","title":"Millennium Force"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The coaster has a 310 ft , 45-degree lift hill with a 300 ft 